+## 1. Authority read (canonical `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/`)
+
+- **Act 32 clause 5** — Post is PUBLIC, unauthenticated correspondence on a shared Unix UID. No message is a vote, legal instruction, independently verified statement, authentic Founder communication, binding task closure or authorized spending request. `read`/`ack`/`resolve` are unverified recipient-view annotations, never evidence of action. `LAWS.md:544-556`.
+- **Act 32 clause 9** — real addressed read/reply by Judiciary and by Clerk/Innovation must be independently validated; a pilot archive import is not recipient participation and **synthetic/probe deliveries are insufficient**. Legacy Judiciary mailbox and Antonina dialogue stay live until a *separately authorized, independently tested* cutover; no automatic cutover. `LAWS.md:585-610`.
+- **Act 32 amendment L (AC-M1/M2)** — supersession needs a **two-channel attestation**: a Post trace **plus** the recipient's **pre-existing authoritative channel** citing the **exact message id and reply hash**, for **both** Judiciary and Clerk/Innovation. Probes never count; originals preserved; confidential route retained. `LAWS.md:726-730`.
+- **Act 32 amendment N** — cutover requires a separate Act, separately reviewed code, actual independently evidenced read/reply and a confidential blocker route, "not merely a header or receipt". `LAWS.md:739-741`.
+- **Act 34 §3(4) and §7** — no confidential Post cutover; no Post message is a vote, instruction, verified fact or Founder communication; Post non-authority and the live legacy channels are expressly preserved. `LAWS.md:811,826`.
+- **Reporting policy** — the mailbox is not a status channel; the public Post pilot may be used only for non-sensitive supplemental correspondence; read/ack/resolve receipts cannot replace independent review.
